# Nothing is declared of `total`. Link types the field by what is stored into it, and the parameter of the head has the type that a read of the field has: whatever is made of it is typed as narrowly as it was when the operand was read out of memory.
# In the typed copy the sum of two whole numbers is of that type by itself, and nothing is assumed.
